{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Promotion Evidence.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Promotion Evidence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"agent promotion evidence agent promotion evidence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Promotion Evidence.md","fileName":"Agent Promotion Evidence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Agent Promotion Evidence","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Promotion Evidence.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Promotion Evidence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"agent promotion evidence agent promotion evidence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Promotion Evidence.md","fileName":"Agent Promotion Evidence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Agent Promotion Evidence","heading":"Agent Promotion Evidence","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Agent promotion should depend on measured behavior rather than enthusiasm for autonomy. Relevant signals include suggestion acceptance, false positives, developer overrides, test results after remediation, mean time to resolution, policy violations, and the frequency of fallbacks or malformed output.\n\nThe pipeline can combine those observations with confidence thresholds, branch restrictions, required reviewers, and environment approvals. A threshold is only one gate: it does not replace validation or human oversight. Promotion is justified when repeated evidence shows that the current scope is reliable and the next scope remains recoverable.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],